n the benchmark to get a more stable reading before deciding. Looking at the broader picture, Round 0 shows a clear 15.2% improvement well above target, while GKR's 2.4% improvement falls short of the 5% threshold.\n\nThe STARK exclusion trace result sits right on the edge—61ms absolute reduction barely clears the 60ms threshold, but the 3.87% percentage falls short of 4%. Let me examine the rollback criteria more carefully to understand how these thresholds interact.\n\nChecking the other conditions: APC 0 actually improved by 32ms rather than regressing, and APC 100 improved by 31ms as well, so both pass. The gains are concentrated in Round 0 with modest improvements elsewhere, so I should present this honestly as a borderline result that technically passes but warrants noting the tight margins.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2704,"cache_read_input_tokens":39592,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2704},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e7b8cdb6-6661-4368-a105-ba06f927c9a9","uuid":"7d855fb7-5b2c-4839-86c9-0ffa3ebf3948"}
